# Runtime env vars for the production container.
#
# This file is the committed TEMPLATE — copy it to `.env.production`,
# fill in the real values, and use it as the source of truth for the
# TWO deployment-time wiring steps the prod runtime needs:
#
#   1. `blocks release secrets sync --file .env.production --yes --json`
#      — syncs the keys + values into the repo's secret set (kept for
#      audit / portal visibility; the running container does NOT read
#      from this set — verified empirically).
#
#   2. Block portal → Build → Trigger (dev environment) → Substitutions
#      — add each non-empty KEY from this file as a substitution. The
#      Blocks release pipeline forwards trigger substitutions as
#      `--build-arg` to buildx; the Dockerfile runtime stage exposes
#      them as ENV so prod-backend.mjs picks them up. This is the ONLY
#      path that reaches the running container.
#
# Once both steps are done, redeploy with:
#
#   blocks release deploy --with-secrets .env.production --wait --json
#   # the --with-secrets is idempotent for step 1; step 2 (substitutions)
#   # is a one-time portal action, not re-applied per deploy.
#
# `.env.production` is gitignored. The same dotenv format is also read by
# the local `vite.config.ts` proxy plugins, so copying values from your
# local `.env` Just Works.
#
# Variable names mirror `.env.example` lines 52-54 / 75 — the dev proxy
# (Vite) and the prod proxy (server/prod-backend.mjs) accept the same
# canonical `AI_GATEWAY_*` names, plus `ANTHROPIC_*` aliases (matching
# Claude Code / Anthropic SDK conventions) as a fallback.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  AI Assistant gateway (Issue Tracker chat panel)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only (no VITE_ prefix). Read by server/prod-backend.mjs.
# `AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN` is a bearer token sent server-side on every
# /api/ai/chat POST; it never reaches the browser bundle.

AI_GATEWAY_URL=
AI_GATEWAY_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Verification backend (Issue Tracker MCP integration — optional)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, /api/verify/* + /api/secrets + /api/evidence + /api/playwright
# forward to this backend. When empty (default), every /api/verify/* call
# returns 503 + {error:"verify_not_configured"} — same behaviour as the
# local Vite proxy when VERIFY_BACKEND_URL is unset, and the production
# bundle's `VITE_USE_REAL_VERIFY` flag is off by default so the in-browser
# mock keeps running.
#
# Leave empty until a real MCP backend is deployed and reachable from the
# Blocks container. The 503 fallback is intentional, not a regression.

VERIFY_BACKEND_URL=
